# ── Runtime data — never bake player records into the image ──────────────
# Elastic Beanstalk containers are ephemeral, so a records file committed to
# the repository or copied into the image is both wrong and misleading: it is
# destroyed on the next deployment. Durable storage is EFS or S3, configured
# at runtime. See NOTICE.md and the run manual.
*-scores.json
ruhrohgue-scores.json
scores.json
/data/
